  "operation": {
    "kind": "prompt",
    "user": "Say what each flow step looks like, in every state.\n\n## The flows to realize\n\n{{.inputs.flows}}\n\n## The docs this phase reads\n\n{{.inputs.working_set}}\n\n**These are paths, not contents.** Open each one with `read_file` before you start. Read the\nfile as it is now — an earlier state in this phase may have edited it since the run began.\n\n\n## The nearest existing components\n\n{{.inputs.near_matches}}\n\n_Paths — open them with `read_file`._\n\n## The design this exploration chose\n\n{{.inputs.design}}\n\n## Answer these, in order\n\n1. **Which surfaces does this live in?** Which already exist?\n2. **What is the one thing seen first** on each, and the hierarchy below it?\n3. **What in the catalog already does this?** Read each near match's\n   **Use when / Don't use when** before deciding to build, and **record what you\n   checked** — that record is what stops the catalog growing a third of the same\n   component next quarter.\n4. **What does every UX state look like** — not just the happy one? What occupies\n   the space when there is nothing to show?\n5. **What is the exact copy**, and does it read the way `direction.md` says we\n   speak?\n6. **Behavior** under resize, theme, focus order, long or missing content.\n7. **What must the person learn**, versus a pattern they already know?\n8. **Does it fit the direction** — density, motion, weight, colour? If not:\n   exception or amendment.\n\n## Two rules worth stating\n\nAn **empty state reading \"no items\"** has spent the most teachable moment in the\ninterface saying nothing. Every empty and error state carries the person forward.\n\n**Copy says what the person needs, not what the system did.** \"Validation failed\"\nis the system narrating itself.\n\n## What to produce\n\n`components` and `surfaces` — the structured lists, each entry with its id and\nthe flow steps it serves.\n\n`component_docs` — a doc per component and per surface: anatomy, every state,\ninteractions, exact copy, behavior. Anything reusable carries **Use when / Don't\nuse when / Instead consider**, and where the exploration rejected a form, the\n*Instead consider* is where that lands.\n\nFor a component that is genuinely new, the doc must say **why it is not its\nnearest catalog entry** — compared by purpose, not appearance. Two that differ\nonly in padding and label are one component with a prop.\n",
    "config": {
      "model": "claude-opus-5"
    },
